# SYNOPSIS

```c
#include <sys/stat.h>

struct stat {
  dev_t st_dev;
  ino_t st_ino;
  nlink_t st_nlink;
  mode_t st_mode;
  uid_t st_uid;
  gid_t st_gid;
  dev_t st_rdev;
  off_t st_size;
  blksize_t st_blksize;
  blkcnt_t st_blocks;
  struct timespec st_atim;
  struct timespec st_mtim;
  struct timespec st_ctim;
};

int stat(const char *__restrict path, struct stat *__restrict st);
int lstat(const char *__restrict path, struct stat *__restrict st);
int fstat(int fd, struct stat *st);
int mkdir(const char *path, mode_t mode);
int chmod(const char *path, mode_t mode);
int fchmod(int fd, mode_t mode);
```

# DESCRIPTION

`stat` fills <st> with the status of the node <path>, `fstat` with that of the open descriptor <fd>.
`lstat` is `stat`: there are no symbolic links.
The fields are filled from what the node says, and the file system keeps no more:

| Field | Value |
| `st_ino` | the node's qid path, unique in its tree |
| `st_mode` | `S_IFDIR | 0755` for a directory, `S_IFREG | 0644` for a file |
| `st_nlink` | 2 for a directory, 1 for a file |
| `st_size` | the size in bytes |
| `st_blksize` | 4096 |
| `st_blocks` | the size in units of 512 bytes, rounded up |
| `st_atim`, `st_mtim`, `st_ctim` | all the node's modification time |
| `st_dev`, `st_uid`, `st_gid`, `st_rdev` | 0 |

Only directories and regular files exist.
`fstat` of 0, 1 or 2 describes an empty regular file.
The header defines `S_IFMT` and the file types, `S_ISDIR`, `S_ISREG` and `S_ISLNK`, the set-id bits and the `S_IRWXU` family of permission bits, with Linux's values; `st_atime`, `st_mtime` and `st_ctime` are the seconds of the times.

`mkdir` makes a directory.
<mode> is ignored.
It fails with `EEXIST` if the name is in use, `ENOENT` if a directory on the path is missing and `ENOTDIR` if one is a file.

There are no permissions to change: `chmod` and `fchmod` succeed if the path or descriptor exists, and change nothing.

All return 0, or -1 with `errno` set.

